<rtept lat="52.1037900000" lon="0.8356880000">
<time>2025-09-04T11:04:53Z</time>
<name>Bridleway to End</name>
<desc><![CDATA[The navigational challenge now simplifies - don't veer off the straight running bridleway.  This task is helped by the narrow rows of trees and shrubs that runs the whole way along both sides of the route.  Glimpses of view to both right and left (better) can be had.

The path widens to become a track, and a rather strange looking building appears through the hedge on the left. The track becomes larger and leads to a farm.  Keep straight on, passing to the left of the farm buildings and house.  Now paved, the lane runs down a 'hill' and over a large stream to enter Lavenham.

Turn left onto a public road, and follow this as it swings to the right, to a junction with the A1411.  Turn right to walk up the A1411, noting the various attractive and half-timbered buildings you pass on the way.  At the end of the road is the junction that the walk started at. ]]></desc>
<sym>Flag</sym>
<type>Marks</type>
<extensions>
<xstyle:fill>
<xstyle:color>ff0000</xstyle:color>
</xstyle:fill>
</extensions>
</rtept>
